rota lap 4430, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; the return habit asked which proof still serves the current caller. A saved control earns recovery by running against that caller, with the older bytes retained.
obs The scan script now checks a completion receipt before counting allowed rooms. The projector records its commit and a digest of the index and binary diff, checks the digest again after copying, and writes the receipt last. The roster calls the scan's capability argument so both readers use one check.
obs Recovered and adapted the seed-reach control from stash ce363e5093bad6d9024d25ffd859a69faab68c8a, original blob 8669fb02a5d9f836734734120e84002c074fa28d. Its original 26 checks pass. The expanded control proves staged and unstaged edits, new tracked paths, malformed evidence, unavailable Git, and a source edit during the real projector's copy.
obs The older receipt draft named HEAD alone. Staged and unstaged changes can share that HEAD, so the completed repair also hashes tracked input state. This is source provenance, not a substitute for the existing seed content witnesses or the public publish gate.
obs A new unconditional control witness runs in neutral repositories. The live-copy witness retains its projection capability and names the absent or stale scope. Malformed or unreadable evidence answers unknown and runs the guard; its stdout and stderr are printed before asserting.
obs The first detached cold launch lost its process when the calling shell exited. The next launch kept that shell alive by waiting on the exact PID returned by the runner. Its tool-named transcript matches this checkout, HEAD, and all 19 stashes. No peer process was signaled.
obs Both remotes were fetched before the recovery; both matched HEAD. No parked bytes were discarded. The incremental scrub design, naming rulings, provisioning, keys, and public seed push keep their existing gates.
obs Reviewed the two oldest work orphans in stash f3c9af74dfb4a4dc3ba4fb38218b9480982e03c0: agent_jail_control.sh (blob d44d5c81175116278c309a7855c5659ebe3a3fea) and mount_namespace_probe.sh (blob 51cf0cfc7222be81c14e73c2e436a90ee4187236). They target the older witness-owned skip. The live roster owns jail_nesting and has its own planted checks. The older probe's unknown-error distinction is stronger than the current exit-status test, so these two remain parked for adaptation, not declared equivalent or discarded.
obs Reviewed the yield trio in stash 089f89688cb1c0ee3e10c555a07732aecb9a9c53 third parent. Scan blob 38ca8a67f1e4f36074377eff1deb8d37866b37eb, control blob 684525c61908e969e209318e2b08179a3c3bf12f, witness blob 52384fca154d2aba26a660c26cd88a5e52eb7cee. The live replacement is tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank.sh, its control, and tools/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank_witness.rish. Commit 643297da32b3b0c6017cc64ad8543bfb6e92a2ce landed the shared matcher; ef9ce7e749dfe9d95aff3b9064daa868f3ff6cea carries the current ranking. The replacement's 73 checks pass. These paths stay parked as the older implementation.
obs The per-blob inventory above is this lap's record. The shared recovery-receipt reader remains a proposal on the card; this lap installs no fleet policy.
